-- ============================================================================
-- PD6 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Flow Assurance, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE LINE IN OPERATION. `relaxationLengthFt`,
-- `steadyStateProfile`, `uForArrivalTemp` and `cooldownTime` are where the
-- fluid, the rate and the clock enter, and they are the four things a flow
-- assurance engineer is actually asked for: how long is this line thermally,
-- what does it arrive at, what insulation would it take to arrive warmer, and
-- how long after a shutdown before it is a problem.
--
-- THE TIER IS BUILT ON ONE SENTENCE: ALL FOUR ARE THE SAME EXPONENTIAL. The
-- energy balance m Cp dT/dx = -U pi D (T - Ta) integrates once and everything
-- in the tier is a rearrangement of it. The relaxation length Lc = m Cp/(U pi
-- D) is the only length scale there is; the number of transfer units is the
-- line measured in those lengths; the arrival is ambient plus the inlet excess
-- times exp(-ntu); the design inverse is the same equation solved for U; and
-- the cooldown is the same exponential in time with M Cp/(U A) in place of Lc.
-- A tier that taught four formulas would have taught three too many.
--
-- WHAT THE TIER MUST NOT PROMISE, AND IT IS HANDED STRAIGHT UPWARD. AN ARRIVAL
-- TEMPERATURE IS NOT A VERDICT. The verdict is the arrival compared against a
-- hydrate temperature the engine does not compute and never will, and on the
-- capstone line the whole margin is 6.524 degF on a boundary that arrived in
-- an email from a laboratory. A margin quoted without the boundary it is
-- measured from has said nothing, and the Expert tier's first finding moves
-- that same arrival across the boundary without touching the boundary at all.
--
-- THREE LIMITS OF THE COOLDOWN, AND THE TIER STATES ALL THREE AS LIMITS.
--
--   THE MASS SLOTS DO NOT MATCH THE LAYER LIST. `overallU` takes as many
--   layers as a line has; `cooldownTime` takes `contents` and `shell` and
--   nothing else. The insulation and the weight coat that carry 56.56 percent
--   of the capstone line's thermal RESISTANCE carry none of its thermal MASS
--   unless the caller lumps them into `shell` by hand. Doing it honestly takes
--   the same line from 2.5446 hr to 5.9523 hr, a factor of 2.3392. Neither
--   number is wrong for what it was asked; only one of them answers the
--   question an operator meant.
--
--   THE START IS NEVER CHECKED AGAINST THE TARGET. `cooldownTime` guards the
--   start against ambient and the target against ambient, and never compares
--   the two with each other. Ask the capstone line for the time to cool from
--   its arrival to the SHUT-IN hydrate boundary, which is the boundary that
--   actually applies once the line packs in, and it returns MINUS 0.5844 hr
--   with ok true, no note, and a station table that runs backwards through
--   negative time and warms up as it goes. The line is already inside that
--   boundary the moment it stops; a negative number of hours is that fact
--   arriving as arithmetic instead of as a refusal.
--
--   AND A LUMPED CAPACITANCE IS A MODEL. One temperature for the fluid, the
--   steel and the coatings together, no axial conduction, no phase change, no
--   convection cell in a shut-in bore. It is the right model for a no-touch
--   time and it is still a model, and the tier says which of its assumptions
--   is the one most likely to bite: the bore-side film that was a short
--   circuit while the line flowed is not one after it stops.
--
-- WHAT THE INVERSE REFUSES, AND THE REFUSAL SAYS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT IT
-- ENFORCES. `uForArrivalTemp` separates two failures that are genuinely
-- different, a target at or below ambient and a target above the inlet, and
-- the module header explains why collapsing them would send an engineer
-- looking in the wrong place. The first refusal then prints "A line cannot
-- arrive above ambient no matter how well it is insulated", which is the
-- opposite of the physics its own guard enforces and contradicts its own
-- second sentence. The Expert tier quotes it verbatim; this tier is where a
-- learner meets it and reads the guard rather than the string.
--
-- The only numbers that travel to the tier above are the line's own stated
-- dimensions, materials and duty. The tier above restates all of them.
-- ============================================================================

values ('flowassurance', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-steady-state","title":"Steady State","lesson_keys":["l01-the-energy-balance","l02-the-relaxation-length","l03-the-arrival-temperature","l04-number-of-transfer-units","l05-what-steady-state-assumes"]},{"key":"m02-designing-to-a-target","title":"Designing to a Target","lesson_keys":["l01-inverting-the-balance","l02-the-u-you-need","l03-what-a-target-costs","l04-what-the-inverse-refuses"]},{"key":"m03-cooldown","title":"Cooldown","lesson_keys":["l01-when-the-flow-stops","l02-the-time-constant","l03-the-no-touch-time","l04-the-mass-the-cooldown-uses","l05-what-a-cooldown-assumes"]},{"key":"m04-the-margin","title":"The Margin","lesson_keys":["l01-how-close-is-close","l02-reading-a-margin","l03-what-moves-it","l04-what-a-margin-does-not-promise"]},{"key":"m05-the-whole-line","title":"The Whole Line","lesson_keys":["l01-one-number-for-a-whole-line","l02-where-the-line-is-coldest","l03-profiles-against-endpoints","l04-what-a-single-arrival-hides","l05-what-the-profile-refuses"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'flowassurance' and tier = 'intermediate';

